WEBVTT

00:00.253 --> 00:01.765
- [Voiceover] What I'd
like to do in this video

00:01.765 --> 00:03.747
is make an informal argument

00:03.747 --> 00:06.446
for why the formula for
the area of a circle

00:06.446 --> 00:09.525
is Pi r squared.

00:09.525 --> 00:10.523
And we're gonna start

00:10.523 --> 00:14.901
just with the most traditional
definition of the number Pi

00:14.901 --> 00:16.563
and that's that and I'll just do it here

00:16.563 --> 00:18.391
in a corner some place

00:18.391 --> 00:21.311
that Pi is equal to the ratio

00:21.311 --> 00:24.110
of the circumference and
the diameter of the circle

00:24.110 --> 00:25.312
or the ratio of the circumference

00:25.312 --> 00:27.143
to the diameter of a circle

00:27.143 --> 00:28.165
or, of course, we could write this

00:28.165 --> 00:29.426
as ratio of the circumference

00:29.426 --> 00:30.937
to, instead of the diameter,

00:30.937 --> 00:32.919
I could write two times the radius

00:32.919 --> 00:35.425
or I can multiply both sides
times two times the radius

00:35.425 --> 00:38.605
and we get our traditional
formula for the circumference,

00:38.605 --> 00:41.708
for the circumference of a circle,

00:41.708 --> 00:44.367
but once again, this literally
just comes straight out

00:44.367 --> 00:46.936
of the definition for the number Pi.

00:46.936 --> 00:49.449
The number Pi is defined as the ratio

00:49.449 --> 00:51.551
between the circumference
and the diameter,

00:51.551 --> 00:53.173
so you just multiply both sides out of it

00:53.173 --> 00:55.845
times the diameter, you
get the circumference

00:55.845 --> 00:59.317
is equal to Pi times the diameter.

00:59.317 --> 01:01.899
Now, we have the circumference
formula right here,

01:01.899 --> 01:04.721
once again, this comes out
of the definition of Pi,

01:04.721 --> 01:07.388
but from this, I'd like to at
least get an intuitive feel

01:07.388 --> 01:11.997
for why the area formula
is given by Pi r squared

01:11.997 --> 01:14.027
and to think about that,
we're going to approximate

01:14.027 --> 01:17.844
the area of polygons,
the areas of polygons,

01:17.844 --> 01:20.213
that are inscribed in a circle.

01:20.213 --> 01:21.835
So over here, I have this, what's this?

01:21.835 --> 01:24.921
There's a five-sided
polygon right over here

01:24.921 --> 01:28.491
and its area is going to be equal to,

01:28.491 --> 01:30.660
so the area of this polygon,

01:30.660 --> 01:32.692
it's going to be five times the area

01:32.692 --> 01:34.017
of each of those triangles

01:34.017 --> 01:36.486
and the area of each of those triangles,

01:36.486 --> 01:39.402
the height is a, the base is b,

01:39.402 --> 01:41.634
so it's going to be base times height

01:41.634 --> 01:46.138
or height times base times 1/2.

01:46.138 --> 01:48.655
So this, once again,
five times ab over two,

01:48.655 --> 01:50.553
it's not that good of an approximation.

01:50.553 --> 01:54.801
This would be the area of
just the inscribed polygon,

01:54.801 --> 01:56.506
so we're definitely underestimating

01:56.506 --> 01:58.251
the area of the entire circle

01:58.251 --> 01:59.853
or leaving out all of these little,

01:59.853 --> 02:01.855
these little chunks
outside of the polygon,

02:01.855 --> 02:03.603
but still inside of the circle.

02:03.603 --> 02:05.835
But as we add more size to the polygon,

02:05.835 --> 02:08.368
we see that we're leaving out less.

02:08.368 --> 02:09.666
We see, when we have now,

02:09.666 --> 02:11.991
this is a one, two, three, four,

02:11.991 --> 02:14.951
five, six, seven-sided polygon,

02:14.951 --> 02:17.971
we're leaving a little bit less.

02:17.971 --> 02:19.696
We're underestimating still,

02:19.696 --> 02:21.474
but we're underestimating by less.

02:21.474 --> 02:22.976
This area that we're giving up

02:22.976 --> 02:26.018
isn't as large as this
area right over here.

02:26.018 --> 02:29.315
So in this approximation,
we have, what did I say?

02:29.315 --> 02:31.257
Seven triangles? One, two, three, four,

02:31.257 --> 02:33.339
five, six, seven triangles.

02:33.339 --> 02:34.901
And the area of each of those triangles

02:34.901 --> 02:38.094
is once again ab over two.

02:38.094 --> 02:41.606
Now, a and b here are different
than a and b over here,

02:41.606 --> 02:43.624
and notice what's happening.

02:43.624 --> 02:45.482
As we increase,

02:45.482 --> 02:48.792
as we increase the number of triangles,

02:48.792 --> 02:52.612
not only is it approximating
the area of the circle better,

02:52.612 --> 02:55.008
but a is getting longer.

02:55.008 --> 02:56.870
And you can see, you could imagine,

02:56.870 --> 02:59.028
as we increase many,
many, many more triangles,

02:59.028 --> 03:01.694
a is going to approach r.

03:01.694 --> 03:05.048
Now another thing to think
about is what is seven,

03:05.048 --> 03:07.377
what is seven times b approaching?

03:07.377 --> 03:09.426
So we're saying that a is approaching r

03:09.426 --> 03:12.268
as we add more of these
sides of the polygon,

03:12.268 --> 03:13.663
as we add more triangles,

03:13.663 --> 03:16.486
now what is the number of triangles

03:16.486 --> 03:19.577
times the base of the triangle,
what is that approaching?

03:19.577 --> 03:22.849
Well this is going to
approach the perimeter of the,

03:22.849 --> 03:24.904
or this is going to be the
perimeter of the polygon,

03:24.904 --> 03:28.585
so seven times b is that plus,

03:28.585 --> 03:30.087
let me actually, let me draw this,

03:30.087 --> 03:33.900
it's that plus that

03:33.900 --> 03:35.014
plus that,

03:35.014 --> 03:35.935
I think you get the point,

03:35.935 --> 03:37.730
plus that,

03:37.730 --> 03:39.519
plus that,

03:39.519 --> 03:41.354
plus that,

03:41.354 --> 03:43.122
plus that.

03:43.122 --> 03:46.893
So once again, seven, let
me write this at seven,

03:46.893 --> 03:50.830
times b, that is the
perimeter of the polygon,

03:50.830 --> 03:52.932
perimeter,

03:52.932 --> 03:57.824
perimeter of the polygon.

03:57.824 --> 03:59.306
So think about what's happening.

03:59.306 --> 04:01.868
As we have more and more
sides of the polygon,

04:01.868 --> 04:06.082
our a, our height of
each of our triangles,

04:06.082 --> 04:09.058
is going to approach our radius,

04:09.058 --> 04:11.955
is going to approach the radius.

04:11.955 --> 04:14.164
It's going to get the height
of each of the triangles.

04:14.164 --> 04:15.165
It's gonna get longer and longer,

04:15.165 --> 04:16.867
it's gonna approach the radius as we have,

04:16.867 --> 04:19.512
as we approach an infinite
number of triangles,

04:19.512 --> 04:22.315
and then the number of polygons we have,

04:22.315 --> 04:23.162
not the number of polygons,

04:23.162 --> 04:26.449
the number of sides we
have times the bases,

04:26.449 --> 04:28.665
that's going to be the
perimeter of the polygon

04:28.665 --> 04:30.657
and as we add more and more sides,

04:30.657 --> 04:31.698
as we add more and more sides,

04:31.698 --> 04:35.348
the perimeter of the polygon
is going to approach,

04:35.348 --> 04:38.781
is going to approach,

04:38.781 --> 04:41.764
is going to approach the
circumference of the circle.

04:41.764 --> 04:44.784
I'll write it out, circumference,

04:44.784 --> 04:46.326
circumference,

04:46.326 --> 04:49.889
and you'll see that even
more clearly right over here.

04:49.889 --> 04:53.845
So, once again, how many
sides do I have here?

04:53.845 --> 04:57.665
I have one, two, three, four, five, six,

04:57.665 --> 05:00.671
seven, eight, nine, 10 sides,

05:00.671 --> 05:03.404
so this, I can write the
perimeter of the polygon

05:03.404 --> 05:06.973
as 10 times b

05:06.973 --> 05:11.344
and then if I multiply
that times a over two,

05:11.344 --> 05:14.047
if I multiply that times,

05:14.047 --> 05:15.391
we'll use another color.

05:15.391 --> 05:17.448
a over,

05:17.448 --> 05:18.938
let me just write it like this,

05:18.938 --> 05:22.421
times a over two,

05:22.421 --> 05:25.792
I'm once again approximating
the area of the circle

05:25.792 --> 05:28.174
'cause a times b over two,

05:28.174 --> 05:31.394
that's the area of each of these triangles

05:31.394 --> 05:33.933
and then I have 10 of these triangles,

05:33.933 --> 05:36.309
but now let's think about
this more generally.

05:36.309 --> 05:39.038
Let's think about it if I were to have n,

05:39.038 --> 05:41.534
if I were to have an n-sided polygon,

05:41.534 --> 05:43.679
so I have n-sided polygon,

05:43.679 --> 05:46.366
then I'd be approximating the area

05:46.366 --> 05:50.480
as n times b,

05:50.480 --> 05:52.441
n times b,

05:52.441 --> 05:53.319
we see this right over here.

05:53.319 --> 05:55.665
When n is equal to 10,
you have 10 times b.

05:55.665 --> 05:58.191
So it's n times b

05:58.191 --> 06:01.861
times a over two.

06:01.861 --> 06:04.373
Times a over two.

06:04.373 --> 06:06.005
I just wrote,

06:06.005 --> 06:07.697
this isn't something mysterious.

06:07.697 --> 06:11.253
The base times the height divided by two,

06:11.253 --> 06:12.197
this right over here,

06:12.197 --> 06:14.517
that's the area of each triangle

06:14.517 --> 06:16.949
and then I'm gonna have
n of these triangles,

06:16.949 --> 06:19.856
so this is our approximation for the area,

06:19.856 --> 06:20.887
so let me write this,

06:20.887 --> 06:24.367
the area is going to be
approximately that right over there.

06:24.367 --> 06:27.656
It's going to be n, the
number of triangles I have,

06:27.656 --> 06:29.685
times the area of each triangle.

06:29.685 --> 06:30.881
Now what's going to happen,

06:30.881 --> 06:33.046
as n approaches infinity,

06:33.046 --> 06:36.546
as I approach having an
infinite sided polygon,

06:36.546 --> 06:38.304
as I have an infinite number of triangles,

06:38.304 --> 06:40.085
so let's just think this
through a little bit.

06:40.085 --> 06:41.216
'cause this is where it gets interesting.

06:41.216 --> 06:43.106
Now this is the informal argument.

06:43.106 --> 06:46.378
To do this better, I'd have to dig out

06:46.378 --> 06:49.032
a little bit of calculus, but
this gives you the essence.

06:49.032 --> 06:50.844
So let's just think about what happens

06:50.844 --> 06:54.069
as n approaches infinity.

06:54.069 --> 06:56.275
So, as n approaches infinity,

06:56.275 --> 06:58.738
we've already said, as we
have more and more sides

06:58.738 --> 07:01.250
and we have more and more triangles,

07:01.250 --> 07:03.221
a approaches r,

07:03.221 --> 07:05.122
so let's write that down.

07:05.122 --> 07:07.773
So, a is going to approach r,

07:07.773 --> 07:11.785
the height of the triangles is
going to approach the radius

07:11.785 --> 07:14.257
and what else is going to happen?

07:14.257 --> 07:18.309
Well, n times b, the
perimeter of the polygon,

07:18.309 --> 07:19.850
the perimeter of the polygon

07:19.850 --> 07:22.102
is going to approach the circumference.

07:22.102 --> 07:23.903
So, a is going to approach r

07:23.903 --> 07:28.385
and n times b is going to
approach the circumference,

07:28.385 --> 07:30.274
is going to approach the circumference,

07:30.274 --> 07:31.816
or another way of thinking about it,

07:31.816 --> 07:33.748
if it's approaching the circumference,

07:33.748 --> 07:37.479
we could say that n times b

07:37.479 --> 07:40.031
is going to approach
two Pi times the radius

07:40.031 --> 07:41.573
'cause that's what the circumference

07:41.573 --> 07:44.163
is going to be equal to.

07:44.163 --> 07:47.245
So, if a is approaching the radius

07:47.245 --> 07:50.736
and nb is approaching two Pi r,

07:50.736 --> 07:53.667
well then, what is the entire,

07:53.667 --> 07:56.668
what is the area of,

07:56.668 --> 07:59.217
what is the area of our polygon

07:59.217 --> 08:03.859
or what is the area of
our polygon going to,

08:03.859 --> 08:06.221
or, the area of our circle going to be?

08:06.221 --> 08:10.452
Well, it is going to approach,

08:10.452 --> 08:13.104
it is going, or I should
say, the area of our polygon

08:13.104 --> 08:14.515
is going to approach,

08:14.515 --> 08:17.417
nb is going to approach two Pi r,

08:17.417 --> 08:19.419
nb is going to approach two Pi r.

08:19.419 --> 08:21.901
Instead of nb, I'm writing two Pi r there.

08:21.901 --> 08:24.142
a is going to approach r.

08:24.142 --> 08:26.433
a is going to approach r,

08:26.433 --> 08:28.725
and then I'm dividing it,

08:28.725 --> 08:31.725
and then I am dividing it by two.

08:31.725 --> 08:33.792
So as n approaches infinity,

08:33.792 --> 08:35.954
as we have infinite number
of sides of our polygon,

08:35.954 --> 08:37.726
an infinite number of triangles,

08:37.726 --> 08:40.428
the area of our polygon
will approach this,

08:40.428 --> 08:42.129
which is equal to what?

08:42.129 --> 08:43.720
Well you have two divided two

08:43.720 --> 08:45.811
and then Pi r times r

08:45.811 --> 08:49.662
is equal to Pi r squared.

08:49.662 --> 08:53.474
So as we approach having
infinite number of triangles

08:53.474 --> 08:55.326
and infinite, I wanna keep that there,

08:55.326 --> 08:57.107
infinite number of sides,

08:57.107 --> 09:00.219
we see that we approach
the area of the circle

09:00.219 --> 09:02.341
and as we approach the area of the circle,

09:02.341 --> 09:04.161
we are approaching Pi r squared.

09:04.161 --> 09:06.023
So hopefully this gives
you an intuitive sense

09:06.023 --> 09:07.414
why this right over here

09:07.414 --> 09:11.759
is the formula for the area of a circle.

09:11.759 --> 09:14.136
You could think about it as the area

09:14.136 --> 09:17.908
of an infinite sided polygon

09:17.908 --> 09:19.470
that is inscribed in the circle,

09:19.470 --> 09:24.042
which will be equal to
the area of the circle.
